"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith=self.webpackChunkdatabricks_monolith||[]).push([[53876],{653876:e=>{e.exports='# Infrastructure Translation\n\nClassic compute clusters carry infrastructure dependencies through cluster-level configuration — init scripts, cluster libraries, spark configs, environment variables, and similar fields attached to the cluster spec. These must be translated into serverless-compatible form before migration.\n\n## Principle\n\n_Within the job config_, the unit of infrastructure translation is a _cluster specification_. A classic job\'s cluster definition — whether shared via `job_clusters[]` or inline under a task\'s `new_cluster` — maps to one serverless `environment` entry. For each cluster-scoped field we support (e.g. `init_scripts`), we translate it into the corresponding field of the environment spec (e.g. for `init_scripts`: a `requirements.txt` referenced from `dependencies`). Tasks that referenced the classic cluster via `job_cluster_key` now reference the new environment via `environment_key` — the many-to-one sharing falls out of replacing the string keys.\n\n## Routing per Cluster-Level Field\n\n| Category                                      | Translatable?              | Next Step                              |\n| --------------------------------------------- | -------------------------- | -------------------------------------- |\n| **Init scripts** (`init_scripts`)             | Yes (scenario-by-scenario) | See [init-scripts.md](init-scripts.md) |\n| **Cluster libraries**                         | Not yet (future)           | Skip, flag to user                     |\n| **Cluster policies** (library-related fields) | Not yet (future)           | Skip, flag to user                     |\n\n## Example: Classic → Serverless\n\n### Before (classic compute)\n\n```json\n{\n  "job_clusters": [\n    {\n      "job_cluster_key": "my_cluster",\n      "new_cluster": {\n        "spark_version": "15.4.x-scala2.12",\n        "num_workers": 2,\n        "node_type_id": "Standard_DS3_v2",\n        "init_scripts": [{ "workspace": { "destination": "/Shared/init-scripts/setup.sh" } }]\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  "tasks": [\n    {\n      "task_key": "main_task",\n      "job_cluster_key": "my_cluster",\n      "notebook_task": { "notebook_path": "/path/to/notebook" }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n### After (serverless)\n\n```json\n{\n  "environments": [\n    {\n      "environment_key": "serverless_env",\n      "spec": {\n        "environment_version": "2",\n        "dependencies": ["-r \\"/Workspace/Shared/serverless-migration/migrated-init-script-deps-a1b2c3d4e5f6.txt\\""]\n      }\n    }\n  ],\n  "tasks": [\n    {\n      "task_key": "main_task",\n      "environment_key": "serverless_env",\n      "notebook_task": { "notebook_path": "/path/to/notebook" }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nKey changes:\n\n- Remove `job_clusters` / `new_cluster`\n- Add `environments` with serverless spec\n- Replace `job_cluster_key` with `environment_key` in tasks\n- For `init_scripts`, see [init-scripts.md](init-scripts.md) — it produces a `requirements.txt` referenced from `dependencies` via a `-r` line\n'}}]);
